# Pagination

Split a long list or short guide into predictable pages when that improves use or performance.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use numbered pages for many similar records and previous/next topic links for a guide. Keep a short list on one page when that is easier to understand.

## When not to use it

Do not use pagination to advance a form or hide critical current information. Avoid infinite scrolling when it prevents keyboard users from reaching the end of the page.

## Home Assistant adaptation

For Home Assistant history, preserve the query, period, filters and sorting when changing page. State how many rows or pages are available. The existing Energy data table uses explicit previous/next buttons for 100-row pages; route-based lists can use the link pattern shown here.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a labelled navigation landmark, descriptive links and aria-current for the current page. Omit a previous link on the first page and a next link on the last. Announce a completed client-side page change and move focus predictably without trapping it.

